  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-65" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;GRIDLIANCE WEST LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;(Dollars in thousands, unless otherwise noted)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Introduction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting that varies from generally accepted accounting principles in the United States of America ("GAAP"). These requirements differ from GAAP related to (1) the presentation of regulatory debits and credits (2) the presentation of deferred income taxes (3) the presentation of regulatory assets and liabilities (4)treatment and presentation of goodwill (5) removal costs. Accordingly, certain footnotes are not prepared on the same basis as the financial statements presented herein. The information below is presented in thousands unless otherwise stated. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements should be read in conjunction with the 2025 FERC Form 1 of GridLiance West LLC. In the opinion of management, all adjustments (consisting of normal recurring accruals) considered necessary for fair financial statement presentation have been made. The results of operations for an interim period generally will not give a true indication of results for the year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-66" contextRef="c-1">Gridliance West LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-67" contextRef="c-1">2026-05-20</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-68" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-69" contextRef="c-1">Q1</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantContingentAssetsOrLiabilitiesTextBlock id="f-70" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:98.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:15pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;1. Organization and Business&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;GridLiance West LLC (&#8220;the Company&#8221;), formed in 2014, is a wholly owned subsidiary of GridLiance Western Holdings LLC (&#8220;GWH&#8221;). GWH is a wholly owned indirect subsidiary of NextEra Energy Transmission, LLC, ("NEET"), which in turn is a wholly owned subsidiary of NextEra Energy Infrastructure, LLC ("NEEI"). NEEI is a wholly owned subsidiary of NextEra Energy Capital Holdings, Inc.("NEECH"), which in turn is a wholly owned subsidiary of NextEra Energy, Inc.("NEE"), a company listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: NEE).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company, a single member limited liability company organized under the laws of Delaware, is a rate regulated transmission provider in Nevada. Its purpose is to collaborate with rural electric cooperatives, municipal utilities, joint action agencies and others to plan for the future of the grid within California Independent System Operator Corp. (&#8220;CAISO&#8221;) located in the United States. The Company invests in necessary electric infrastructure and implements strategies to improve system reliability and resiliency and reduce overall costs to customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantContingentAssetsOrLiabilitiesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAmountsRelatedToUtilityPlantAdjustmentsTextBlock id="f-71" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:30.208%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:98.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2. Regulatory Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Formula Rate Filings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company principally generates revenue through transmitting electricity to its customers. Substantially all of the Company&#8217;s material revenue streams consist of FERC-approved, tariff-based revenue and is settled by CAISO. Under the Company&#8217;s formula rate, all revenue credits, including revenue related to pole attachment agreements, are deducted from the gross revenue requirement to calculate the net revenue requirement for the year. The Company recognizes revenue from the transmission of electricity proportionally throughout the year based on the FERC-approved TRR as calculated prior to the beginning of each year (the &#8220;Rate Year&#8221;) using the FERC-approved formula rate template. CAISO bills load-serving customers for actual usage based on the TRR and estimated load. Differences between the billed rates and TRR are recorded to the TRBA. The TRBA, with an annual adjustment filed with FERC, ensures that all transmission revenue credits and adjustments for any over- or under-recovery of the annual TRR flow through to transmission customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Following a Public Letter Ruling issued by the Internal Revenue Service in April 2017, FERC initiated a proceeding into the methodology used by the Company (and various other public utilities) for calculating accumulated deferred income taxes (&#8220;ADIT&#8221;) balances in its projected test year and annual true-up calculations for the transmission formula rates. Subsequently, FERC issued an order in December 2018 directing the Company to revise its formula rate template to adopt FERC&#8217;s revised methodology to calculate ADIT balances in its transmission formula rates. In March 2019, the FERC approved the Company&#8217;s revisions to its formula rate template to adopt the FERC&#8217;s proposed ADIT methodology. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Following the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017 (&#8220;TCJA&#8221;), FERC issued an order in November 2019 directing utilities to revise their formula rate templates to revise their calculation of ADIT to account for the tax rate changes caused by the TCJA. The Company submitted its filing in April 2020, which is still pending Commission approval as of the filing date.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 29, 2019, FERC instituted a proceeding pursuant to Federal Power Act section 206 to examine the Company&#8217;s recovery of an income tax allowance in its formula rate template. The Commission found that the Company&#8217;s recovery of an income tax allowance may result in an unjust double recovery of income taxes as described in the D.C. Circuit&#8217;s United Airlines decision and FERC&#8217;s Revised Policy Statement on Treatment of Income Taxes. The Commission set this issue for hearing and settlement proceedings. On July 29, 2019, the Company filed an offer of settlement to resolve the income tax allowance issue. As part of that offer of settlement, the Company&#8217;s existing income tax allowance was set at a negotiated percentage of 72.13% through June 30, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2020 and then set at 53.29% effective July 1, 2020. Further, the Company&#8217;s base ROE of 9.6% was subject to a rate moratorium until July 1, 2020, such that no settling party could request any changes to the base ROE to become effective prior to the expiration of the moratorium. On September 5, 2019, the Settlement Judge certified the uncontested settlement for FERC&#8217;s approval, which the Commission approved on December 19, 2019. On February 19 and April 29, 2020, the Company filed revised tariff sheets to reflect the Income Tax Allowance calculations, and FERC issued letter orders approving them on October 13, 2021.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Pursuant to the Income Tax Settlement referenced above, the Company is obligated to adjust the mechanism in its formula rate template to recover its income tax allowance if an upstream change in control materially impacts the underlying basis for the settled income tax allowance percentages. NEET&#8217;s acquisition of 100% of the upstream ownership interests in the Company satisfies this condition. As such, on April 1, 2021, the Company has revised its formula rate template to allow for 100% recovery of the Company&#8217;s income tax allowance. On May 20, 2021, FERC approved the Company's Filing, effective May 31, 2021.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Other Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On July 19, 2023, the Company submitted a request with FERC to recover 100% of all prudently incurred costs associated with its investment in two projects approved by the CAISO Board of Directors on May 18, 2023, the GLW/VEA Area Upgrades and the Beatty 230 kV Project, in the event that either project is ultimately abandoned for reasons outside of the Company's control. The Commission granted the Company's request on August 30, 2023. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On August 3, 2023, the Company submitted an application pursuant to section 204 of the Federal Power Act requesting authorization to issues long-term debt securities as well as waiver from the Commission&#8217;s competitive bidding and negotiated placement requirements. The Commission issued an order authorizing the issuance of such securities on September 29, 2023.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On April 29, 2024, the Company submitted a request with FERC for incentive rate treatment pursuant to Order No. 679, for its investment in the GLW/VEA Area Upgrades ("the Project"). Specifically, the Company requested authorization to include in rate base 100% of prudently incurred Construction Work in Progress ("CWIP") related to the Project&#8217;s development. The Commission granted the Company's request in Docket No. ER24-1865-000 on June 28, 2024 effective June 29, 2024. Since CWIP in rate base during the construction period is considered an acceleration of a return on the allowance for funds used during construction, the Company believes that prior to the Project going into service, CWIP in rate base is recorded as an Alternative Revenue Program (&#8220;ARP&#8221;), with any over or under collection reflected as a regulatory asset or liability. The income statement offset is reflected within revenue from regulatory mechanisms. Through March 31, 2026, the Company has recognized $14,976 related to this program.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In the fourth quarter 2025, the Company submitted applications to the Public Utility Commission of Nevada ("PUCN") under the Utility Environmental Protection Act ("UEPA") for permits to construct 230 kV substation improvements and associated facilities to interconnect several generation projects to the existing Trout Canyon Substation.UEPA applications were approved in the first quarter of 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAmountsRelatedToUtilityPlantAdjustmentsTextBlock>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-72" contextRef="c-1">Gridliance West LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-73" contextRef="c-1">2026-05-20</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-74" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-75" contextRef="c-1">Q1</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfRateTreatmentWhereUnamortizedLossOnReacquiredDebtAndUnamortizedGainOnReacquiredDebtAccountsAreNotUsedTextBlock id="f-76" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;3. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company entered into Corporate Support Services Agreements with subsidiaries of NextEra Energy whereby the costs incurred in connection with corporate and administrative services performed under these agreements, including but not limited to corporate oversight, human resources, records management, risk management, and payroll services, are charged to the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In addition, certain plant, property, and equipment, including leasehold improvements, office furniture and equipment, computer hardware and software, and prepaid expenses (together the &#8220;Common Use Assets&#8221;), are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;held by subsidiaries of NextEra Energy but are used by the Company. A portion of the charges related to the Common Use Assets is allocated to the Company based on the &#8220;Direct Charge&#8221; allocation methodology.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfRateTreatmentWhereUnamortizedLossOnReacquiredDebtAndUnamortizedGainOnReacquiredDebtAccountsAreNotUsedTextBlock>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-77" contextRef="c-1">Gridliance West LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-78" contextRef="c-1">2026-05-20</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-79" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-80" contextRef="c-1">Q1</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfRetainedEarningsRestrictionsTextBlock id="f-81" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;4. Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Commitments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Construction Contract Commitments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has executed construction contract commitments related to the build-out of projects in Nevada. As of March 31, 2026, the Company had outstanding purchase obligations of $644,309 for the purchase of materials, services, and equipment, in which the company expects to settle through 2032.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Surety Bonds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;As of March 31, 2026, the Company had $9,600 in outstanding bonds securing commitments related to the Company transmission facilities (lines and stations).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Litigation and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Legal Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company currently does not have any significant outstanding litigation matters or claims. When the Company determines that an unfavorable outcome or loss of a particular matter is probable, and the amount of the loss can be reasonably estimated, a liability for the contingent obligation is recognized, as well as any expected insurance recovery amounts up to the accrued loss. As new information becomes available as a result of activities in such matters, conclusions regarding the probability of outcomes and estimated loss may change. The impact of subsequent changes to accruals may have a material effect on results of operations reported in a single period. The Company expenses all legal fees in the period the expenses are incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfRetainedEarningsRestrictionsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfInterimDisclosureTextBlock id="f-82" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;5. SUBSEQUENT EVENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's management has evaluated the recognition and disclosure of subsequent events for its March 31, 2026 financial statements through May&#160;20, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfInterimDisclosureTextBlock>
