    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The CAISO tariff provides for a true-up mechanism in which the CAISO calculates any over-collection or under-collection of transmission revenues to the authorized revenue requirement and either credits or charges that difference to transmission customers in the subsequent year. In addition, any wheeling revenues received are included in the calculation and effectively refunded to the transmission customer over the subsequent year. The Transmission Revenue Balancing Account balance was $0.0 million and $3.8 million over-collected as of March 31, 2026 and December 31, 2025, respectively.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Charges based on annual Transmission Revenue Requirement as approved by the FERC.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
